  "details": "- CVE-2026-126714: always truncate session files before writing to prevent corrupted session data\n- CVE-2026-127960: fix quadratic time when concatenating folded HTTP response headers\n- CVE-2026-128064: use TLS for mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URL schemes\n- CVE-2026-128090: refuse keyless phar signatures when an OpenSSL public key exists\n- CVE-2026-129289: drain unread request bodies to prevent FastCGI request smuggling\n- CVE-2026-129291: remove FPM worker stdio pipe events before closing them to prevent a use-after-free in the master\n- CVE-2026-129292: escape request method, auth user and script name on the FPM status page\n- CVE-2026-129496: fix DATEG(tzcache) use-after-free when logging errors during startup\n- CVE-2026-129506: keep the SOAP DTD alive during XML cleanup to prevent a use-after-free\n- CVE-2026-129538: fix PATH_INFO underflow in CGI init_request_info()\n- CVE-2026-15353: fix out-of-bounds read on empty SOAP-ENC:arraySize",
